onfirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Place Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-19","committee":"Audit & Governance Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"People Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Health Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Policy and Resources Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-16","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"People Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Cabinet Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"The Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Health Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.southend.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Council allocates \u00a38.0 million capital receipts for transformation with benefits to be developed and validated through future governance processes.","lead":"The council is deploying a material amount of capital receipts upfront without yet having finalised business cases or confirmed the savings outcomes that justify the expenditure, creating execution risk around financial sustainability.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Flexible Use of Capital Receipts Strategy 2026-27","paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72691/72691.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Planned merger with Castle Point and Rochford to form South East Essex Council formally stopped following LGR pause on 7 September 2026.","lead":"A major disruption to the council's operational planning mid-strategy requires the transformation programme to be justified on standalone grounds rather than as LGR preparation.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Flexible Use of Capital Receipts Strategy 2026-27","paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72691/72691.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Retrofit project depends on securing \u00a3930k grant from Warm Homes Wave 3, currently under application","lead":"Grant dependency creates a funding contingency; if the application is unsuccessful, a larger share of the retrofit cost will fall to HRA reserves","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Housing Retrofit and Resettlement Update","paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72589/72589.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"The Council","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Flexible Use of Capital Receipts Strategy 2026-27","paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72691/72691.pdf","headline":"Council allocates \u00a38.0 million capital receipts for transformation with benefits to be developed and validated through future governance processes.","detail":"The council has committed \u00a38.0m of capital receipts to three transformation areas: workforce restructuring (\u00a33.5m), corporate transformation capability (\u00a32.0m), and digital/technology transformation (\u00a32.5m). The paper explicitly states that 'The precise financial benefits will develop as individual projects progress through discovery, design and implementation' and will be validated through normal financial governance before incorporation into the MTFS.","category":"capital","matters":"The council is deploying a material amount of capital receipts upfront without yet having finalised business cases or confirmed the savings outcomes that justify the expenditure, creating execution risk around financial sustainability.","figures":"\u00a38.0 million total identified; \u00a33.5m workforce restructuring, \u00a32.0m corporate transformation capability, \u00a32.5m digital, data, cyber and technology","quote":"The precise financial benefits will develop as individual projects progress through discovery, design and implementation. Savings and benefits will therefore continue to be validated through the Council's normal financial and transformation governance before being incorporated into the MTFS.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"The Council","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Flexible Use of Capital Receipts Strategy 2026-27","paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72691/72691.pdf","headline":"Planned merger with Castle Point and Rochford to form South East Essex Council formally stopped following LGR pause on 7 September 2026.","detail":"The government paused its decision to create five unitary councils for Greater Essex on 7 September 2026, and Southend's merger work has been formally stopped. The council had aligned its transformation strategy with preparation for this reorganisation, so the pause requires new justification for the transformation programme.","category":"governance","matters":"A major disruption to the council's operational planning mid-strategy requires the transformation programme to be justified on standalone grounds rather than as LGR preparation.","figures":"7 September 2026","quote":"For Southend-on-Sea, this means that all work to create a new unitary council comprising of Southend-on-Sea, Castle Point and Rochford has now been formally stopped.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"The Council","paper_title":"Housing Retrofit and Resettlement Update","paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72589/72589.pdf","headline":"Retrofit project depends on securing \u00a3930k grant from Warm Homes Wave 3, currently under application","detail":"The retrofit program is seeking up to \u00a3930k external grant funding to match the Council's \u00a3550k reserve contribution. This grant application remains pending and not yet confirmed.","category":"other","matters":"Grant dependency creates a funding contingency; if the application is unsuccessful, a larger share of the retrofit cost will fall to HRA reserves","figures":"\u00a3930,000","quote":"Notes the ongoing application for up to \u00a3930,000 of additional grant funding through the Warm Homes: Social Housing Fund Wave 3.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"The Council","paper_title":"Housing Retrofit and Resettlement Update","paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72589/72589.pdf","headline":"\u00a3951k from existing budgets committed over 2026/27 to 2029/30 to acquire 6 new temporary accommodation homes","detail":"The Council allocated \u00a3951k from Housing Pressures Action Plan budgets across four years to acquire 6 new council homes for temporary accommodation and resettlement, intended to reduce reliance on expensive nightly lets.","category":"capital","matters":"Multi-year capital commitments for housing assets affect forward spending capacity and demonstrate how budget reserves are being deployed across the spending plan","figures":"\u00a3951k, 6 homes, budget spanning 2026/27 to 2029/30","quote":"Agrees to use \u00a3951k from the existing Housing Pressures Action Plan budgets from 26/27 \u2013 29/30 for match funding Local Authority Housing Funding to acquire 6 new Council homes for temporary accommodation and resettlement purposes.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"The Council","paper_title":"Housing Retrofit and Resettlement Update","paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72589/72589.pdf","headline":"\u00a3550k drawn from HRA Capital Reserves for retrofit match funding in 2026/27","detail":"Cabinet agreed to use up to \u00a3550k from HRA Capital Reserves to provide match funding and contingency for retrofitting 93 council homes to EPC C standard. The retrofit is expected to deliver annual fuel savings averaging \u00a3321 per home.","category":"reserves","matters":"Reserve depletion for capital projects directly affects HRA financial flexibility and cash available for other purposes or contingencies","figures":"\u00a3550k, \u00a3321 per home annual saving, 93 homes","quote":"Agrees to use up to \u00a3550k from the Housing Revenue Account (HRA) Capital Reserves for 2026/27 for match funding and contingency costs in order bring the project forward and retrofit 93 council homes.","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-14"},"name":"Southend-on-Sea UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Council allocates \u00a38.0 million capital receipts for transformation with benefits to be developed and validated through future governance processes.","lead":"The council is deploying a material amount of capital receipts upfront without yet having finalised business cases or confirmed the savings outcomes that justify the expenditure, creating execution risk around financial sustainability.","also":["86 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Policy and Resources Overview & Scrutiny Committee on 2026-10-08","n_findings":87,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Flexible Use of Capital Receipts Strategy 2026-27","top_paper_url":"https://southend.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s72691/72691.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":160,"news_drafts_total":3}}